# AXIS CELL: predicate INPUT = GUARDEDNESS. This is the only artefact in the
# liveness net that samples the GUARDED value of the `arm.guard is None` test
# inside `match_has_catch_all` (self_host_typechecker/typecheck.gg); every other
# cell, and every text pin in `tests/lints.rs`, leave that input unsampled.
#
# The only catch-all arm (`case x if g:`) carries a guard, so it does NOT
# guarantee a match: `main` passes `g == false` and `n == 7`, control falls out
# of the `match` with `s` still moved, and `print(s)` is a use-after-move --
# rejected by `gg check` with `error[E_UseAfterMove]`.
#
# RED-VERIFY (drop the guard test): delete `if arm.guard is None:` from
# `match_has_catch_all` and de-indent its `match`. That edit preserves the
# signature, preserves the conservative tail `return false`, mentions none of
# `ctx`/`types`/`exhaust`, and touches no call site -- so the signature pins, all
# three argument pins, both body pins AND every other outcome cell in this net
# are measurably blind to it: `cargo test --test lints
# self_host_match_fallthrough_predicates_pinned` stays GREEN under it. Rebuild
# the driver. Measured: this cell flips rc 1 -> rc 0, 4359 bytes of C, with
# every other cell and the whole lint GREEN.
# If this cell does not go red under that break, STOP -- the fixture's guard is
# not being consulted.
void sink(String ^x):
    pass

void probe(int n, bool g):
    String s = "hello"
    sink(^s)
    match n:
        case 1:
            s = "a"
        case x if g:
            s = "b"
    print(s)

void main():
    probe(7, false)
